=== Scenario 13 (FABRIC TEST-NETWORK): (A) read-time compatibility for
=== pre-v3.3 legacy records, version 3.4, sequence 9; (B) insufficient
=== peer endorsement. Produced by
=== scripts/scenario_13_legacy_compatibility_and_endorsement_live.sh
=== against the same three-organisation Fabric test-network used
=== throughout this dissertation. Unedited console output below (ANSI
=== colour codes stripped only).
===
=== Part A closes a gap this dissertation identified immediately after
=== v3.3 shipped: a record written before v3.3 has no custodianMsp key at
=== all, so CustodianMSP unmarshals to empty on read. AUTH-NEG-TEST is
=== not a synthetic example -- it is a genuine component registered under
=== v3.0 during Scenario 9 (2026-08-29), long before CustodianMSP,
=== InstalledInProductID, or DealerID existed, and it has never been
=== assembled or delivered since, so its legacy "owner" field still holds
=== a real, usable MSP.
===
=== Part B closes a gap explicitly stated as untested throughout this
=== dissertation's Discussion and Limitations sections: "a transaction
=== deliberately submitted with insufficient peer endorsements was not
=== evaluated."

=== 1-5. Package, install, approve, and commit v3.4/sequence 9 ===
