### PART B: insufficient peer endorsement ###
############################################################
--- Register a fresh component with only ONE organisation's peer address (--peerAddresses localhost:7051 only; the committed policy requires more) ---
2026-08-31 02:07:33.756 BST INFO [chaincodeCmd] ClientWait -> txid [824e7a866178cc6c2996659b5112b6de2c4d55d1841dd39b526e1c3ad3ac3202] committed with status (ENDORSEMENT_POLICY_FAILURE) at localhost:7051
Error: transaction invalidated with status (ENDORSEMENT_POLICY_FAILURE) - proposal response: <nil>

--- Confirm the component was NOT created (query should fail: no state committed) ---
Error: endorsement failure during query. response: status:500 message:"no token found for INSUFFICIENT-ENDORSE-1 (GetState returned nil)"

*** The ordering service accepted and sequenced the transaction (it was
*** assigned a real txid and included in a block), but every peer
*** independently validated it against the committed endorsement policy
*** during the commit phase and marked it ENDORSEMENT_POLICY_FAILURE,
*** so it was never applied to the world state. This is Fabric's own
*** execute-order-validate model rejecting an under-endorsed transaction
*** exactly as designed, confirmed live rather than assumed from the
*** platform literature.

=== DONE: Scenario 13 complete. Both previously-stated gaps -- pre-v3.3
=== legacy-record readability, and insufficient-endorsement rejection --
=== are now confirmed with real evidence rather than left as untested
=== caveats. ===
